# ♻️ Smart Recycle Bin – Hardware Documentation

## 1. Introduction

The hardware part of the Smart Recycle Bin project is designed to automate waste disposal using sensors, a microcontroller, and a motor-controlled lid.

The system is intended to work with the machine learning software to allow recyclable items to be detected before the bin opens.

## 2. Hardware Components

| No. | Component | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Arduino Uno | Controls hardware operations |
| 2 | HC-SR04 Ultrasonic Sensor | Detects objects or measures distance |
| 3 | Servo Motor (SG90) | Opens and closes the bin lid |
| 4 | Camera / Webcam | Captures waste images |
| 5 | Laptop / PC | Runs the machine learning model |
| 6 | 5V Power Supply | Supplies power to the components |
| 7 | Connecting Wires | Connects electronic components |
| 8 | Recycle Bin | Holds recyclable waste |

*Note: This is the proposed hardware configuration. Confirm the components against your actual prototype.*

## 3. Hardware Connection

### Arduino Uno Pin Configuration

| Component | Arduino Pin |
|---|---|
| Ultrasonic VCC | 5V |
| Ultrasonic GND | GND |
| Ultrasonic TRIG | D9 |
| Ultrasonic ECHO | D10 |
| Servo Signal | D6 |
| Servo VCC | External regulated 5V |
| Servo GND | Common GND |

### Camera Connection

The camera is connected to the laptop or computer through USB. Python uses the camera to capture images for machine learning classification.

### Power Supply

- Arduino Uno can receive power through USB.
- The servo motor should use a suitable external regulated 5V supply.
- Connect the external supply ground to Arduino GND.
- Do not power a high-current servo directly from the Arduino 5V pin.

## 4. Working Principle

1. The ultrasonic sensor detects an object near the bin.
2. The camera captures an image of the object.
3. The Python machine learning model analyzes the image.
4. The model identifies whether the object is a bottle or not.
5. The classification result can be communicated to the Arduino.
6. If the object is accepted, the servo motor opens the bin lid.
7. After disposal, the lid closes automatically.

The camera-based classification and Arduino communication must be integrated for the complete automated workflow.

